          human: "Quebec Rummy (Rami QuÃ©bÃ©cois) is a regional variation of Contract Rummy played extensively in French-speaking Canada. It is characterized by its specific sequence of 7 or 11 rounds of 'Contracts' and its unique rules regarding 'Buying' from the discard pile (The 'Pige'). Like other contract variants, players must fulfill exactly what the round calls forâ€”sets or runsâ€”before they can expand their melds. It is a social game often played at family dinners (les grandes tablÃ©es) with multiple decks to accommodate large groups.",
